# the raw file bytes — the exact carve-out gap this residual closes. `blob_backed?/1` itself
# is unchanged (still referenced, still true), so the sweep's routing is what breaks. Flips
# the governed-purge proof (after the sweep `Storage.get(key)` still returns the bytes instead
# of :not_found) while the row IS still deleted and the audit/ref-count arms are untouched.
